<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · South America</p><h1 class="st-title">Socialist Republic of Chile</h1><p class="st-meta">1932 CE – 1932 CE · capital Santiago</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Chilean socialist republic proclaimed by military officers in June 1932, which lasted only twelve days before a counter-coup.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-chile">Chile</a> was hit severely by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-depression">Great Depression</a>, which collapsed nitrate and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a> exports. On 4 June 1932 the air force commander <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marmaduke-grove">Marmaduke Grove</a> and other officers, with the politicians <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carlos-davila">Carlos Dávila</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eugenio-matte">Eugenio Matte</a>, overthrew President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-esteban-montero">Juan Esteban Montero</a> and proclaimed the Socialist Republic of Chile.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>A governing junta announced radical measures, including the dissolution of Congress, the distribution of land, the release of goods pawned by the poor, and plans to nationalise key industries. Divisions quickly emerged between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marmaduke-grove">Grove</a>'s more radical socialism and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carlos-davila">Dávila</a>'s moderate state socialism. Opposition from the army and conservative groups grew.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>On 16 June 1932 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carlos-davila">Dávila</a> ousted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marmaduke-grove">Grove</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eugenio-matte">Matte</a>, who were exiled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/easter-island">Easter Island</a>. Dávila ruled until September, and after further instability, elections in October 1932 returned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arturo-alessandri">Arturo Alessandri</a> to the presidency of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-chile">Republic of Chile</a>. Grove later helped found the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/socialist-party-of-chile">Socialist Party</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/socialist-republic-of-chile.jpg" alt="Socialist Republic of Chile" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: See file history below for details. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Chile.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1932 CE – 1932 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Santiago</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Marmaduke Grove, Carlos Dávila</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Roman Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Spanish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/chile">Chile</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>República Socialista de Chile</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1932&amp;focus=socialist-republic-of-chile" aria-label="Socialist Republic of Chile on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2875 3391 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Socialist Republic of Chile lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M3195 3647L3195 3647"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M3195 3647h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3195 3647h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M3195 3647h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Santiago. <a href="/atlas?year=1932&amp;focus=socialist-republic-of-chile">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

